## Editor

{{if eq .EditorMode "standard" -}}
You are using the built-in **standard** editor: keys always type into the
buffer and editing commands are triggered with modifier chords, so there is
no separate command mode to switch into.

Learn more in the [standard editor guide](https://docs.rune.build/learn/standard-editor).
{{- else if eq .EditorMode "helix" -}}
You are using the built-in **helix** editor: a motion first selects the text
you mean, then an operator acts on that selection, so you press `w` then `d`
rather than `dw`. There can be many selections at once: `C` copies the
selection onto the next line, `s` selects every regex match inside it, and
every motion, operator and insert-mode key then acts on all of them.

Learn more in the [helix editor guide](https://docs.rune.build/learn/helix-editor).
{{- else if eq .EditorMode "exo" -}}
You are using an **exo** editor: Rune hands editing off to your own external
editor (for example Vim or Neovim) while keeping its windows, tabs, and
commands around it.

Learn more in the [exo editor guide](https://docs.rune.build/learn/exoeditor).
{{- else -}}
You are using the built-in **vim** editor: like vi, you switch between a
normal mode for navigation and commands and an insert mode for typing into
the buffer.

Learn more in the [vim editor guide](https://docs.rune.build/learn/vim-editor).
{{- end}}

